/-
This module formalizes the Brockian Framework, establishing the connection between the golden ratio φ and prime number distribution through geometric methods. It includes definitions and theorems for the Golden Monad, Pentagon Structure, Brockian Spiral, Prime Embedding, Brockian Character, Pentagonal Averaging, Brockian Zeta Function, and a spectral approach to the Goldbach Conjecture. Key results include the fundamental embedding theorem (‖spiralPrime(p)‖ = p) and the conditional Goldbach theorem based on a spectral model.
-/

import Mathlib

set_option linter.mathlibStandardSet false

